# Recrypt Licensing

Copyright © 2026 Identikey Inc. (https://identikey.io)

Recrypt is a monorepo with a per-crate license split. Check the `license`
field in each crate's `Cargo.toml` for the authoritative answer.

## Core library crates — MIT OR Apache-2.0

The core cryptography and protocol crates are permissively licensed under
your choice of the [MIT License](LICENSE-MIT) or the
[Apache License 2.0](LICENSE-APACHE):

- `crates/recrypt-core` — hybrid encryption (KEM-DEM)
- `crates/recrypt-ffi` — OpenFHE + liboqs FFI bindings
- `crates/recrypt-openfhe-sys` — low-level OpenFHE bindings
- `crates/recrypt-wire` — wire protocol (Gordian Envelope + Bao)
- `crates/recrypt-storage` — S3-compatible storage client
- `crates/recrypt-client` — client library
- `crates/identikey-auth` — hardware-backed identity (Secure Enclave / TPM)

Use them anywhere, commercially or otherwise, no strings attached.

## Deployable stack — AGPL-3.0-or-later (or commercial)

The recryption proxy and the tooling around it are licensed under the
[GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later](LICENSE-AGPL), with a
commercial license available for uses the AGPL doesn't fit — see
[LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md](LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md):

- `recrypt-server` — recryption proxy server
- `recrypt-cli` — command-line interface
- `crates/identikey-storage-auth` — storage auth service

## Third-party components

Vendored dependencies under `vendor/` (e.g. OpenFHE — BSD-2-Clause,
liboqs — MIT) are distributed under their own licenses, which continue to
apply to that code.

## Contributions

Contributions are accepted under the Contributor License Agreement in
[CLA.md](CLA.md), which is what makes the dual-licensed portion possible.
